{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) is requesting implementation of srd056-cp requirements R2.1 through R2.4 in the `cmd/cp` utility. This is a stitch task (Task ID: 5392) in a generation run. The specific requirements are:\n   - **R2.1**: `-r` or `-R` or `--recursive` must copy directories recursively, preserving directory structure.\n   - **R2.2**: Without `-r`, must refuse to copy a directory and print an error to stderr (partially implemented already).\n   - **R2.3**: `-L` or `--dereference` must follow symlinks in SOURCE, copying the file they point to.\n   - **R2.4**: `-P` or `--no-dereference` must preserve symlinks as symlinks rather than following them. `-P` is the default when `-r` is used.\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/cp/main.go` and `cmd/cp/cp_test.go`. Acceptance criteria require compilation, passing tests, and go vet clean.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU `gcp`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Recursive directory copying with `filepath.Walk` or manual traversal\n   - Symlink handling: `os.Lstat` (no-dereference) vs `os.Stat` (dereference)\n   - `os.Readlink` + `os.Symlink` for preserving symlinks\n   - Flag parsing is manual (no cobra for cmd/ utilities), handling both short and long flags\n   - `ExpectedFiles` in DiffTest for verifying filesystem state\n   - Normalizers for stderr differences between Go and GNU binaries\n   - The `-P` flag is the default behavior when `-r` is active (symlinks preserved as symlinks in recursive mode)\n   - Without `-r`, default is to dereference symlinks (follow them)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd056-cp.yaml**\n     - Full SRD for cp utility with R1-R4 requirement groups\n     - R2.1-R2.4 are the target requirements for this task\n     - Non-goals include: --reflink, --sparse, -u, --backup, --context\n     \n   - **cmd/cp/main.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Currently implements R1.1-R1.4 (basic copy, -i, -f, -n flags)\n     - Key structures: `overwriteMode` enum, `owDefault/owAskUser/owNoClobber`\n     - Global vars: `owMode`, `unlinkDest`, `stdinReader`, `errDeclined`\n     - Functions: `main()`, `parseFlags()`, `applyFlag()`, `applyLongFlag()`, `copySingle()`, `copyMultiple()`, `copyFile()`, `doCopy()`, `confirmOverwrite()`, `fmtPathErr()`\n     - Already has directory-is-source error: `fmt.Errorf(\"-r not specified; omitting directory '%s'\", src)` in `copyFile()`\n     - Uses `os.Stat` (dereferences symlinks) throughout\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"bufio\"\n         \"errors\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"io\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"path/filepath\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     type overwriteMode int\n     const (\n         owDefault  overwriteMode = iota\n         owAskUser                // -i\n         owNoClobber              // -n\n     )\n     var (\n         owMode      overwriteMode\n         unlinkDest  bool\n         stdinReader = bufio.NewReader(os.Stdin)\n         errDeclined = errors.New(\"declined\")\n     )\n     // ... (see full file in conversation above)\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/cp/cp_test.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Currently tests R1.1-R1.4 with differential tests against gcp\n     - Uses normalizers: `normBin` (binary name), `normCase` (lowercase), `normTry` (filter \"try\" lines)\n     - Has `writeFile` helper\n     - Test sub-groups: r1_1_