ogic in the directory copying function—this handles cases where the destination directory already exists, either from a previous copy operation or when copying a source into an existing target directory.  If the destination exists as a regular file instead, `os.Mkdir` would fail with a different error that we'd correctly propagate back. Since `src` is always a real directory at this point (symlinks are handled separately), using `os.Stat` to get its permissions for the destination is the right approach. Time to implement this in main.go.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17983,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17983},"output_tokens":34,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e8c1df5-4d5a-4189-b399-4532c255aaa7","uuid":"8ea9b183-4439-4d7b-9db6-fc9bbcf51fdb"}
